From e7071547b478c70eb6ee0bdafaffb03df8735c7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:07:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: let the DRM HAL use /data/mediadrm, as stock EMUI
 did

Huawei's Widevine engine (a legacy plugin of android.hardware.drm@1.0-
service) keeps its files in /data/mediadrm/IDM<uid>/ like every
pre-Treble Widevine build; stock EMUI 8's vendor policy allowed hal_drm
there. Without it the engine could not initialise (OEMCrypto_Initialize
failed, every session "General DRM error").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 sepolicy/hal_drm_default.te | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sepolicy/hal_drm_default.te

diff --git a/sepolicy/hal_drm_default.te b/sepolicy/hal_drm_default.te
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1a3609a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sepolicy/hal_drm_default.te
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# Widevine: Huawei's engine (stock EMUI 8, a legacy plugin in /vendor/lib/mediadrm loaded by
+# android.hardware.drm@1.0-service) keeps its files in /data/mediadrm/IDM<uid>/, like every
+# pre-Treble Widevine build. Stock EMUI's vendor policy allowed the DRM HAL there (hal_drm,
+# media_data_file); without it the engine cannot initialise and every session fails.
+allow hal_drm_default media_data_file:dir create_dir_perms;
+allow hal_drm_default media_data_file:file create_file_perms;
-- 
2.53.0

